{"school":{"dbn":"17K352","name":"Ebbets Field Middle School","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"17","district_label":"District 17","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":152,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"46 MCKEEVER PLACE, BROOKLYN, NY 11225","phone":"929-457-6230","website":"www.EFMS352.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/73471","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"Ebbets Field Middle School is Equity driven STEAM learning Community that encourages and supports our students to be self-starters, creative thinkers, and innovators of their own pathways. We provide students with project-based hands-on learning experiences that engage our students in explorations that challenge them to think critically. We are a school community that believes in providing our students enriching experiences in the ARTS through music and visual arts. We have extensive partnerships with BRIC Museum, Brooklyn Connections through the Public Library, Project Lead the Way, Ifetayo Cultural Center, I WILL Graduate, 7 Mindful Habits and No Place for Hate. ALL students have the opportunity to participate in our Afterschool Program through New York Edge where students can enjoy sports (basketball, soccer, volleyball) activities, dance/cheerleading/step, public speaking, leadership development, martial arts, performing arts and STEM activities. Our students showcase Broadway Jr. Performances each year and we have performed Fame Jr., Lion King Jr., and Newsies. We also support students social and emotional development through weekly Advisory programming, onsite Mental Health Services, Student Peer Mentoring, LGBTQ group, monthly community meetings. We believe in the power of student voice through our Student Government. We believe in collaborations and partnerships with our families and staff in supporting the academic and social emotional growth of our students.","start_time":"0